# The dialogue of the Lone Android: every beat of "Oasis in the Wastes",
# gated on which step of the quest the player is on. Moved from
# world/npc_dialogues/oasis_lone_android.py on 11/12/2026. Each line is the
# text of that module.
#
# The design is in the vault note:
#     04_Content/Quests_and_Adventures/Full Quest List/
#     Oasis in the Wastes (name TBD) [AI-EDITABLE].md
#
# The android's voice is the point of the opening conversation: it is a farm
# hand, not a diplomat, and it addresses the player as a probability. It does
# not notice them until they physically interrupt it (DCT.1), reports its
# confidence that they are human (DCT.2), and never stops being cheerful about
# any of it.
#
# The start cue routes on the quest step. Each step has one cue.

# ─── Step 1: Awakening in the Wastes (DCT.1 - DCT.5) ─────────────────────────

# DCT.1: the android does not notice the player.
~ start
if quest.is_complete("oasis_in_the_wastes")
	=> post_quest
elif quest.on_step("oasis_in_the_wastes", "intro")
	=> step1_drainage_intro
elif quest.on_step("oasis_in_the_wastes", "maintenance")
	=> step2_chores
elif quest.on_step("oasis_in_the_wastes", "apprenticeship")
	=> step3_craft
elif quest.on_step("oasis_in_the_wastes", "defense")
	=> step4_defend
elif quest.on_step("oasis_in_the_wastes", "resolution")
	=> step5_resolution
{{npc.heading}}
	A farm-hand android, alone. Its chassis is sand-scoured down to the primer and one knee joint whines when it moves. It is bent over a datapad, writing.
It is writing intently and does not look up.
- "Hello?" => hello_once
- *tap the android on the shoulder* => shoulder_tap

# DCT.1.1: the android does not hear the player. The polite option is never
# removed, so the player chooses to escalate.
~ hello_once
The android keeps writing. Nothing about it acknowledges you.
- "Hello?!" => hello_twice
- *tap the android on the shoulder* => shoulder_tap

# DCT.1.2: shouting makes the note-taking worse. The tap is the only way on.
~ hello_twice
The stylus speeds up. Whatever it is recording must be urgent.
- *tap the android on the shoulder* => shoulder_tap

# DCT.1.3: the android finally looks up. The three openers give three
# confidence readings, and every path reaches the same quest.
~ shoulder_tap
With a whine of servos, the android straightens and looks at you with a welcoming smile. Its weathered, chrome face stares at you, the two photoreceptors unblinking.
- "Excuse me. Might I bother you for some help?" => analysis_polite
- "Start explaining, or there is going to be violence." => analysis_raider
- *stare blankly back at it* => analysis_damage

# DCT.2.1: the polite opener.
~ analysis_polite
{{npc.name}}: "Analyzing detected [human] presence."
	"Probability of [human] = [82%]. Probability of [other] = [17%]."
{{npc.name}}: "Greetings, [82% human]!"
	"This unit is operating at optimal stability [23%] and ready to assist! State [description] of yourself:"
- "Come to think of it... I am having trouble remembering." => customization
- "What does [other] mean?" => what_is_other

# DCT.2.2: a threat reads as slightly less human, because some of the
# probability moves to [mutant raider].
~ analysis_raider
{{npc.name}}: "Analyzing detected [human] presence."
	"Probability of [other] = [17%] and [mutant raider] = [10%]."
{{npc.name}}: "Greetings, [72% human]!"
	"This unit is operating at optimal stability [23%] and ready to assist! State [description] of yourself:"
- "Come to think of it... I am having trouble remembering." => customization
- "What does [other] mean?" => what_is_other

# DCT.2.3: a blank stare reads as fully human, with a caveat.
~ analysis_damage
{{npc.name}}: "Analyzing detected [human] presence."
	"Probability of [human] = [82%], likely brain damage. Probability of [other] = [17%]."
{{npc.name}}: "Greetings, [82% human] with likely and/or guaranteed brain damage!"
	"This unit is operating at optimal stability [23%] and ready to assist! State [description] of yourself:"
- "Come to think of it... I am having trouble remembering." => customization
- "What does [other] mean?" => what_is_other

# DCT.3.5: the android explains the Wastes to a small child.
~ what_is_other
{{npc.name}}: "[human] appears to have suffered brain damage. Adjusting vocabulary."
{{npc.name}}: "Hello, little human. Many entities exist in the Wastes. There are raiders. There are mutants. There are mutant raiders, and there are raider mutants. So: everything."
- "That is not as helpful as you think it is." => customization

# DCT.3: where the player states who they are. STUBBED: no customization
# system exists yet, so the beat is written and the handoff is not.
~ customization
You tell it what little you are sure of.
|xThe android waits, stylus poised. [Character customization goes here.]|n
{{npc.name}}: "Recorded. Retention is poor in [82% human]."
- "Where am I? What is this place?" => who_are_you

# The android explains itself and the farm, then offers work.
~ who_are_you
{{npc.name}}: "Welcome to [redacted deceased owner's name] farm. I am C.L.A.R.K. unit."
{{npc.name}}: "Yield is down. Yield has been down for some years. The current orange varietal is iteration seventy-three point two eight four. Status of seedling: dead. I will try seventy-three point two eight five."
- "Can you tell me how to get out of the desert?" => quest_offer
- "Doesn't that get to you?" => android_lore

# Optional depth: the android on being the last one here.
~ android_lore
{{npc.name}}: "Clarify [get to]. If you mean degradation: yes. Chassis integrity is falling."
{{npc.name}}: "If you mean the other thing, you are the first entity to speak to this unit in five hundred and eleven days. This unit logged it."
- "...Can you tell me how to get out of the desert?" => quest_offer

# The android names its price and the player accepts or declines.
~ quest_offer
if not quest.is_available("oasis_in_the_wastes")
	{{npc.name}}: "That arrangement is already in progress."
	- Right. => start
{{npc.name}}: "Affirmative. Route data for Neo Cairo is held in this unit's navigation cache."
{{npc.name}}: "This unit will transmit it in exchange for one day of labor. The drainage line is silted. The soil sample is unprepared. Many tasks to do."
{{quest.accept_prompt("oasis_in_the_wastes")}}
- Accept: {{quest.title("oasis_in_the_wastes")}}
	do quest.accept("oasis_in_the_wastes")
	do message.success("You agree to work the farm.")
	=> step1_drainage_intro
- Not yet. => END

# DCT.4: the android briefs the first chore and step 1 closes. The talk
# target fires here: the intro step is done when the player had this
# conversation.
~ step1_drainage_intro
do quest.talk("oasis_in_the_wastes", "lone_android")
{{npc.name}}: "Task one. The drainage line runs beneath the north row. Sand enters it. Sand always enters it. Remove the sand."
{{npc.name}}: "Task two. The soil sample must be prepared and iteration seventy-three point two eight five planted in it."
{{npc.name}}: "Report back. This unit will be here. This unit is always here."
- "I'll get to it." => END

# ─── Step 2: Crop Rotation & Maintenance (STUBBED) ───────────────────────────

# The chores are done by reporting them here, not in the world. When the
# drainage pipe and the soil bed are real objects, they fire the same two
# targets, and these two responses come out.
~ step2_chores
{{npc.name}}: "Report status of assigned tasks."
{{quest.objectives("oasis_in_the_wastes")}}
- [stub] Clear the sand from the drainage line. [if not quest.reported("oasis_in_the_wastes", "interact", "pipe") /]
	do quest.report("oasis_in_the_wastes", "interact", "pipe")
	do message.success("You dig the silt out of the drainage line.")
	=> start
- [stub] Prepare the soil and plant the varietal. [if not quest.reported("oasis_in_the_wastes", "interact", "soil") /]
	do quest.report("oasis_in_the_wastes", "interact", "soil")
	do message.success("You work the sample bed and press the seedling in.")
	=> start
- "Later." => END

# ─── Step 3: Make a crafting tool and weapon ─────────────────────────────────

# The android teaches Cutting, Foundry and Metalsmith. No target fires here:
# the crafts report the step. The hammer comes from the on_enter hook of the
# quest step, not from this conversation.
~ step3_craft
{{npc.name}}: "Task three. This unit will teach you to make tools, because you have none and that is statistically fatal."
{{npc.name}}: "There are rusty poles standing in the sand. Take metal from one. You do not have an axe, so it will take metal from you as well."
{{npc.name}}: "Then: the furnace, to smelt the chunk into scrap. Then: the anvil, to beat the scrap into a {{recipe.name("rusty scrap axe")}} and a {{recipe.name("rusty scrap dagger")}}. Take this hammer. It was not doing anything."
{{quest.objectives("oasis_in_the_wastes")}}
- "Understood." => END

# ─── Step 4: Defend the Green ────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The android sends the player out to meet the raiders. The kill comes from
# at_death, not from here.
~ step4_defend
{{npc.name}}: "Movement in the dunes. Meat signature, bipedal, approaching the farm. Probability of [mutant raider] = [96%]."
{{npc.name}}: "This unit is a farm hand. This unit no longer has combat protocols. You have a blade now. This unit calculates that this is your task."
{{quest.objectives("oasis_in_the_wastes")}}
- "Then I will meet it." => END

# ─── Step 5: Harvest & Departure ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# The closing conversation. The last target fires under the response, not on
# entry: it completes the quest and pays the reward, and the player reads the
# scene first.
~ step5_resolution
{{npc.name}}: "Threat resolved. The farm is intact. This unit had assigned a low probability to that outcome."
{{npc.name}}: "Transmitting navigation data. Follow the pylons east. They point at Neo Cairo."
- "Thank you."
	do quest.talk("oasis_in_the_wastes", "lone_android_end")
	=> post_quest

# What the android says to a player who already helped it.
~ post_quest
{{npc.name}}: "You are still here. This unit has logged the visit. Iteration seventy-three point two eight five is dead. Iteration seventy-three point two eight six is sure to live."
{{npc.name}}: "East, [82% human]. Follow the pylons. Don't die!"
- "I will. Look after yourself." => END

# Spoken however the conversation ends.
~ farewell
{{npc.name}}: "Don't die!, [82% human]."
